      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T07:33:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As Remi and I discussed in the meeting, the 20 seconds delay is a rough estimate of whether a service is cached. This is because we don\u0027t have a way to get the real status from mdnsresponder, and we don\u0027t want to change the code because it\u0027s going to be deprecated. However, I did measure the time it takes to get a cached service from mdnsresponder, and it was less than 10 seconds. Therefore, I believe that 20 seconds is a realistic number to use to measure if a service is cached.",
